<%#
  A transformed ancestor becomes the containing block a fixed descendant resolves
  against, so the sidebar lays out inside this box rather than over whatever else the
  group's shared page is rendering. The height is what its inset-y-0 then measures,
  and it's short enough that the menu scrolls as a column the way a laptop's does.

  The rail it collapses to under a 1100px-wide preview pane is the component reading the
  window, not this box -- widen the window, or open the preview standalone
%>

<div class="tw:relative tw:h-[560px] tw:transform-gpu">
  <%= render(component) %>
</div>
